# BixBench bix-5-q1 — Analysis report (disease vs control, Issy ASXL1 fibroblasts)

## Data
- featureCounts: 60,662 genes x 16 samples; 14 annotated in coldata (7 disease, 7 control; sex F10/M4).
- MGD1640F, MGD1641F excluded (no condition annotation).
- Pre-filter total >= 10 across the 14 samples -> **31,149 genes tested**.
- Size factors via median-of-ratios (range 0.855–1.458, geometric mean 1).

## Model
DESeq2-style NB GLM (pure-Python implementation):
dispersion per gene by Cox-Reid adjusted NB profile likelihood over a grid,
empirical-Bayes shrinkage toward a dispersion~1/mean trend; final NB GLM (IRLS,
log link, offset=size factors); Wald test; BH (FDR) across tested genes.

## Results (condition-only, primary — STABLE)
- DEGs padj<0.05 & |log2FC|>=1 : **418** (up 262, down 156)
- DEGs padj<0.05 (no LFC cut)  : **442**
- Top genes (by padj): UGT3A2, FRRS1L, VANGL2, TXLNGY(chrY), EIF1AY(chrY), DDX3Y(chrY),
  CNTN4, IGSF3, NSUN7, KDM5D(chrY), CNTN6, PI16, ALX4, XKR6, GNAO1, STMN2, TNFSF18 ...
- 16 DEGs are chrY (sex-linked), driven by the male imbalance (disease 1M vs control 3M).

## Sensitivity: sex-adjusted (~sex+condition) — DEGENERATE on this design
- Single male in disease group (cell n=1) -> perfect separation; MLE of the disease
  coefficient is infinite for a large fraction of genes.
- 6,020/31,149 genes (19.3%) pinned at the |LFC| cap (+-36); median condition-only
  |LFC| of those genes = 0.13 with median padj ~ 1.0 => NOT genuine disease effects.
- Corr(sex-adjusted LFC, condition-only LFC) ≈ 0.007; Jaccard of DEG sets = 0.055.
- => sex-adjusted model is statistically unusable here; condition-only is the
  reliable model for the DEG set used in any downstream enrichment.

## GO BP enrichment — BLOCKED in this environment
Evidence (concrete):
- No DNS/network (pypi.org, ftp.ebi.ac.uk fail: no name resolution); pip install of
  pydeseq2/gseapy/goatools/mygene fails with "No matching distribution".
- No R/Rscript binary anywhere on the filesystem -> cannot run Bioconductor
  DESeq2 / clusterProfiler / org.Hs.eg.db.
- Exhaustive filesystem scan found NO GO annotation source: no *.gaf, gene2go,
  go.obo/go-basic, GO.db, org.Hs.eg.db, MSigDB c5, nor "GO:" strings in any data
  directory or installed packages.
- gencode "ont" column is entirely NaN; no functional annotation in any input file.
Conclusion: a statistically valid ORA GO-BP (Fisher exact, background = all measured
genes with GO BP annotation) requires an external human GO BP -> gene table, which is
NOT present and NOT obtainable here. Per instructions, NO GO enrichment results were
fabricated. DEG lists are delivered ready for GO mapping by approved HGNC symbol.

